---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { DISCLAIMER_FULL, MASTHEAD_NAME } from '../lib/constants';
import { getRelease } from '../lib/data';
import { withBase } from '../lib/paths';

const release = getRelease();
---

<BaseLayout
  publicationRequiresApprovedClaims={false}
  title="Legal"
  currentPath="/legal/"
  description="Medical, copyright, AI, and privacy disclaimer."
  showDisclaimer={true}
>
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="legend-label">Legal</div>
    <h1>Disclaimer, licensing, privacy</h1>
  </section>

  <section class="page-section wrap-prose">
    <h2 class="sec">Medical disclaimer</h2>
    <p>{DISCLAIMER_FULL}</p>
    <p>
      If you are in medical distress, seek emergency care. Nothing on this site establishes a doctor–patient
      relationship with any contributor or AI system.
    </p>

    <h2 class="sec">Creator and independence</h2>
    <p>
      Created and maintained by <strong>Justin Wojciechowski</strong> (
      <a href="https://github.com/justinwojo" rel="noopener noreferrer">@justinwojo</a>
      ). Independent community research project. Justin is not a clinician. This site is{' '}
      <strong>not</strong> operated by, affiliated with, or endorsed by Drift0r. It is published with Drift0r’s
      permission; <strong>permission is not endorsement</strong>. There is no financial relationship with or
      compensation from Drift0r. See <a href={withBase('/about/')}>About</a> for the full statement.
    </p>

    <h2 class="sec">AI-generated content</h2>
    <p>
      Multi-agent analysis is used as a research aid. AI output can be wrong, incomplete, or fabricated.
      Multi-model agreement is not clinical validation. Always verify against primary literature and clinical
      records before acting.
    </p>
    <p class="record-note">
      Models disclosed for this content version: {(release.ai_models_disclosed || []).join('; ')}.
    </p>

    <h2 class="sec">Copyright and literature</h2>
    <p>
      Original project content is intended for MIT licensing with the repository. Third-party works keep their
      own licenses. Bibliographic metadata and short attributed quotations may appear; paywalled publisher
      PDFs and unlicensed full texts are not redistributed. Local research PDFs are not published on this site.
    </p>

    <h2 class="sec">Privacy and consent</h2>
    <p>
      Patient materials in the research repository were publicly released in de-identified form for community
      help. A purpose-built website is a new, persistent publication and requires explicit scope approval.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>Current status:</strong> patient approval <span class="mono">{release.patient_approval.status}</span>.
      {release.patient_approval.notes}
    </p>
    <p>
      Broad patient permission allows publication at the owner’s editorial discretion. This candidate still
      uses the neutral masthead <span class="mono">{MASTHEAD_NAME}</span> and does not publish the private
      approval correspondence. Consent does not establish clinician review or third-party copyright clearance.
    </p>

    <h2 class="sec">Indexing</h2>
    <p>
      Indexing is controlled by release metadata field <span class="mono">noindex</span> (currently{' '}
      <span class="mono">{String(release.noindex)}</span>). {
        release.noindex ? (
          <>
            Every page serves HTML <span class="mono">noindex, nofollow</span> and the provenance bar reports
            indexing disabled.
          </>
        ) : (
          <>
            Every page serves HTML <span class="mono">index, follow</span> and the provenance bar reports indexing
            enabled.
          </>
        )
      }{' '}
      The site <span class="mono">robots.txt</span> permits crawlers to <em>fetch</em> pages so they can read that
      meta directive — it does not use a blanket <span class="mono">Disallow: /</span>. Patient permission for
      publication does not by itself enable indexing; the release field is the sole control.
    </p>

    <h2 class="sec">Contact / corrections</h2>
    <p>
      Material errors in research content are logged through the repository corrections process and listed on
      the changelog and on affected records rather than applied silently. There is <strong>no public privacy
      email address</strong> for this project.
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Correction, privacy, or removal requests:</strong> open a structured GitHub issue using the
        template <span class="mono">Correction, privacy, or removal request</span> (see{' '}
        <a href={withBase('/about/contribute/')}>How to contribute</a>
        ). <strong>Do not post private medical records</strong> or personal identifiers in the issue.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Public research contributions:</strong> structured GitHub Issues for literature suggestion,
        factual/citation correction, contradictory evidence, or alternative hypothesis — same contribute page.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Sensitive consent or withdrawal from Drift0r:</strong> may continue through the{' '}
        <strong>existing private correspondence channel</strong> with the repository owner (not a public issue
        and not a published email address).
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2 class="sec">Withdrawal of consent</h2>
    <p>
      The patient (Drift0r) may revoke publication consent at any time through the{' '}
      <strong>existing private correspondence channel</strong> with the repository owner, or by filing a
      removal request via the public GitHub template above without attaching private records. On confirmed
      revocation the owner will set release status to <span class="mono">revoked</span>, begin site and
      repository takedown under owner control within a <strong>7-day</strong> target, and log the change.
      Forks, mirrors, and search caches are outside complete control; removal will be requested where practical.
    </p>
  </section>
  <div style="padding-bottom: 48px;"></div>
</BaseLayout>
